# Build context exclusions for worker/Dockerfile.
#
# The image needs only worker/, services/ and requirements.txt. Everything here
# would otherwise be copied into the build context and slow the upload down; the
# env files are excluded for a harder reason — secrets must never be BAKED into an
# image layer, because `docker history` would reveal them to anyone who can pull
# it. Supply them at run time instead (`docker run --env-file` or the platform's
# dashboard).

# Secrets — never in an image
.env
.env.*
frontend/.env*

# The website is not part of the worker image
frontend/
api/
backend/
dist/
dist-remote/
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
vite.config.js
vercel.json

# Local/editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
logs/
data/
tests/
tools/
*.bat
README.md
